  "note": "What every function outside the module can do when module code calls it, for tools/testshape. A package's default covers every function and method of it; an entry under functions overrides it, keyed Name, Type (all its methods), Type.Method, or Type.Field (a spawner field). A key ending /... covers every package under that path that has no entry of its own. Classes: none (touch-free); a comma list of store, git, proc, net, fs, clock; dispatching (it calls back what was registered with it or handed to it), alone or in the list; spawn:N (argument N is the program it runs); spawn:field. Where it is unsure whether a function touches, it is classified as touching: every approximation errs away from unit. A callback handed to an outside function needs no dispatching class: the module code that hands it takes it as a value, which makes it reachable. An interface method is keyed Interface.Method in the package that declares the interface; a call module code makes through an outside interface is charged by that entry. A handle's touch (a file, a connection) is charged where it is acquired, so the reads and writes through io's interfaces are none.",
